  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "44115830",
      "title": "Setting Up Custom Two-Way Binding",
      "lectureOrder": 148,
      "videoOrder": 140,
      "sourceHash": "4ec023ae6b23aa7dac9c098c420dfd6983d4d7e5add19a4c40c31160c42c3e40",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.72,
          "end": 2.31,
          "en": "So the goal now",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.31,
          "end": 7.31,
          "en": "is to set up our own two-way bindable property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.71,
          "end": 10.41,
          "en": "in one of our own components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.41,
          "end": 13.98,
          "en": "And for that, I created a brand new project,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.98,
          "end": 15.81,
          "en": "you find it attached.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.81,
          "end": 17.55,
          "en": "And it's a very simple project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 17.55,
          "end": 19.86,
          "en": "with a very simple app component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 19.86,
          "end": 22.74,
          "en": "where I'm outputting some inputs here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 22.74,
          "end": 26.22,
          "en": "to allow the user to enter some width and height value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 26.22,
          "end": 29.61,
          "en": "And where I then have one custom component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 29.61,
          "end": 33.933,
          "en": "this RectComponent, which outputs a rectangle.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 34.89,
          "end": 38.76,
          "en": "And currently, the width and height of that rectangle",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 38.76,
          "end": 41.67,
          "en": "are set with those dynamic style bindings,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 41.67,
          "end": 44.88,
          "en": "but they are set to hardcoded values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 44.88,
          "end": 47.913,
          "en": "and that will change over the next minutes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 48.9,
          "end": 52.08,
          "en": "There also is a onReset method here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 52.08,
          "end": 53.97,
          "en": "which currently isn't doing anything.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 53.97,
          "end": 56.16,
          "en": "Because it's now in this component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 56.16,
          "end": 59.34,
          "en": "where I wanna make the size of this rectangle",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 59.34,
          "end": 61.35,
          "en": "two-way bindable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 61.35,
          "end": 64.98,
          "en": "so that we can pass new width values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 64.98,
          "end": 67.59,
          "en": "into this RectComponent from outside it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 67.59,
          "end": 71.457,
          "en": "So from inside the app component to this RectComponent.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 71.457,
          "end": 75.3,
          "en": "But so that we also get notified about changes here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 75.3,
          "end": 76.62,
          "en": "in the app component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 76.62,
          "end": 78.33,
          "en": "so that we can update the values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 78.33,
          "end": 80.4,
          "en": "that are shown in those inputs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 80.4,
          "end": 83.16,
          "en": "so that the input width and height values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 83.16,
          "end": 86.55,
          "en": "are always in sync with the width and height values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 86.55,
          "end": 88.35300000000001,
          "en": "that are used for rectangle.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 89.49,
          "end": 92.28,
          "en": "Now currently, if you run NPM install",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 92.28,
          "end": 95.52000000000001,
          "en": "and you start this development server with NPM start,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 95.52000000000001,
          "end": 98.43,
          "en": "you'll see a page that looks something like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 98.43,
          "end": 100.35,
          "en": "And currently changing the width",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 100.35,
          "end": 102.15,
          "en": "and height here in these inputs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 102.15,
          "end": 104.91,
          "en": "won't have any effect on that rectangle,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 104.91,
          "end": 107.283,
          "en": "but that's what we'll work on soon.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 108.6,
          "end": 109.92,
          "en": "I also wanna highlight",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 109.92,
          "end": 114.21000000000001,
          "en": "that I am already using two-way binding with ngModel",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 114.21000000000001,
          "end": 116.07,
          "en": "here in the app component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 116.07,
          "end": 118.47,
          "en": "And here, I'm using it in the way you've seen it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 118.47,
          "end": 120.03,
          "en": "many times before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 120.03,
          "end": 122.01,
          "en": "I have some property here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 122.01,
          "end": 124.95,
          "en": "here, I'm not using signals, but I could do,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 124.95,
          "end": 128.58,
          "en": "but here I got an object property with a width and height",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 128.58,
          "end": 131.55,
          "en": "and I'm binding the width and height in that object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 131.55,
          "end": 133.14,
          "en": "with two-way binding.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 133.14,
          "end": 136.05,
          "en": "But of course, this is no custom two-way binding",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 136.05,
          "end": 138.87,
          "en": "instead, this is two-way binding with ngModel",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 138.87,
          "end": 141.3,
          "en": "as you've seen it many times before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 141.3,
          "end": 143.34,
          "en": "But now we're going to make",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 143.34,
          "end": 146.4,
          "en": "this RectComponent two-way bindable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 146.4,
          "end": 150.45,
          "en": "And specifically there, I wanna accept some size property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 150.45,
          "end": 152.463,
          "en": "that should be two-way bindable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 153.3,
          "end": 155.16,
          "en": "So let's do that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 155.16,
          "end": 157.86,
          "en": "So the goal is to have a size property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 157.86,
          "end": 159.63,
          "en": "in this RectComponent,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 159.63,
          "end": 163.59,
          "en": "which should accept values from outside this component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 163.59,
          "end": 167.133,
          "en": "So it should be configurable from outside this component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 168.12,
          "end": 172.26,
          "en": "And typically, you would do that with the input decorator",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 172.26,
          "end": 174.18,
          "en": "or with help of the input function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 174.18,
          "end": 176.43,
          "en": "And that is what I'll do here as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 176.43,
          "end": 179.643,
          "en": "So I'll turn this size property into an input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 181.14,
          "end": 182.88,
          "en": "I'll also define its type.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 182.88,
          "end": 186.03,
          "en": "And here, I expect to get an object as a value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 186.03,
          "end": 187.47,
          "en": "which should have a width,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 187.47,
          "end": 190.35,
          "en": "which should have a value type of string,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 190.35,
          "end": 192.663,
          "en": "and a height, which will also be a string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 193.5,
          "end": 195,
          "en": "Since these will be the values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 195,
          "end": 197.583,
          "en": "that are entered into the input fields.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 199.38,
          "end": 202.07999999999998,
          "en": "Now I also wanna make sure that this is always set.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 202.07999999999998,
          "end": 205.11,
          "en": "So I will set this to be required",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 205.11,
          "end": 207.21,
          "en": "and I'll add this exclamation mark here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 207.21,
          "end": 208.92000000000002,
          "en": "to make it clear to TypeScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 208.92000000000002,
          "end": 212.04,
          "en": "that this property will always have a value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 212.04,
          "end": 214.893,
          "en": "even though we don't assign an initial value here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 217.11,
          "end": 220.82999999999998,
          "en": "So that is the size I expect to get.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 220.82999999999998,
          "end": 224.82,
          "en": "And of course, with that size set from outside,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 224.82,
          "end": 227.22,
          "en": "we can go to the template of this component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 227.22,
          "end": 229.47,
          "en": "and now set the width and height here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 229.47,
          "end": 231.273,
          "en": "on this div dynamically.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 232.29,
          "end": 236.25,
          "en": "By accessing size.width here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 236.25,
          "end": 241.023,
          "en": "and combining that with just px to get a pixel value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 242.16,
          "end": 245.853,
          "en": "and then here, I'll have size.height.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 247.77,
          "end": 249.903,
          "en": "That should set the width and height.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 250.8,
          "end": 254.13,
          "en": "Of course, we now must make sure that in app component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 254.13,
          "end": 257.85,
          "en": "we do bind that size property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 257.85,
          "end": 262.85,
          "en": "And for that, we wanna pass this rectSize property here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 263.07,
          "end": 267.063,
          "en": "as a value for this size property to app-rect.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 268.74,
          "end": 271.08,
          "en": "If you do all that and you save that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 271.08,
          "end": 272.76,
          "en": "you should have an application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 272.76,
          "end": 276.27,
          "en": "where now this cube here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 276.27,
          "end": 279.42,
          "en": "is in the end kind of connected to the app component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 279.42,
          "end": 281.4,
          "en": "And if I change the width here, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 281.4,
          "end": 285.63,
          "en": "you see that now the dimensions of this rectangle",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 285.63,
          "end": 286.683,
          "en": "change with it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 287.88,
          "end": 292.02,
          "en": "So that's good. We got one-way binding now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 292.02,
          "end": 295.5,
          "en": "We're updating the dimensions of this rectangle",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 295.5,
          "end": 297.093,
          "en": "with help of this input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 298.38,
          "end": 300.51,
          "en": "But now I also wanna make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 300.51,
          "end": 302.82,
          "en": "that when we click this rectangle,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 302.82,
          "end": 305.79,
          "en": "we trigger this onReset method here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 305.79,
          "end": 309.45,
          "en": "and in there, I wanna reset this rectangle",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 309.45,
          "end": 311.88,
          "en": "to some fixed dimensions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 311.88,
          "end": 314.22,
          "en": "So I wanna change this.size",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 314.22,
          "end": 317.73,
          "en": "and set it to some new dimensions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 317.73,
          "end": 320.64,
          "en": "But this is not how we should do it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 320.64,
          "end": 323.25,
          "en": "because size is just an input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 323.25,
          "end": 327.09,
          "en": "It's not meant to communicate back to the component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 327.09,
          "end": 329.043,
          "en": "that passed the input value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 330.03,
          "end": 332.64,
          "en": "Instead for that, we need that two-way binding",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 332.64,
          "end": 334.29,
          "en": "I'm talking about.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 334.29,
          "end": 336.99,
          "en": "And to set this up with decorators,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 336.99,
          "end": 339.45,
          "en": "so with the input decorator being used,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 339.45,
          "end": 344.22,
          "en": "we have to add a second property to this RectComponent",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 344.22,
          "end": 347.67,
          "en": "and decorate that with the output decorator",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 347.67,
          "end": 349.77,
          "en": "because two-way binding in the end",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 349.77,
          "end": 353.04,
          "en": "is the combination of input and output.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 353.04,
          "end": 356.763,
          "en": "We're accepting value, but we're also updating a value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 358.17,
          "end": 361.14,
          "en": "So we need an output as well as an input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 361.14,
          "end": 363.03,
          "en": "And now what's important",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 363.03,
          "end": 367.11,
          "en": "is that this output must have a very specific name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 367.11,
          "end": 369.27,
          "en": "for Angular to understand",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 369.27,
          "end": 373.32,
          "en": "that you want to have a two-way bindable property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 373.32,
          "end": 376.8,
          "en": "Because you now must use the same property name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 376.8,
          "end": 379.02,
          "en": "as you used for the input,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 379.02,
          "end": 381.903,
          "en": "but then add change at the end of it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 383.46,
          "end": 385.59,
          "en": "And this is now not up to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 385.59,
          "end": 388.68,
          "en": "This output must be named like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 388.68,
          "end": 390.69,
          "en": "for Angular to understand",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 390.69,
          "end": 393.72,
          "en": "that this input and output belong together",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 393.72,
          "end": 398.72,
          "en": "and together create a two-way bindable size property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 398.97,
          "end": 402.46,
          "en": "Then you still create an EventEmitter here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 403.40999999999997,
          "end": 406.71,
          "en": "and you define the data that will be emitted.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 406.71,
